        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Neoregelia, Aloysia\n- Taxonomy: Bromeliaceae, Bromelioideae\n- Places: South American rainforests, the Americas\n- Topics: native range, climate distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Neoregelia is a genus of flowering plants in the bromeliad family Bromeliaceae and the subfamily Bromelioideae.\n- Neoregelia is native to South American rainforests.\n- Aloysia is native to the Americas.\n- Aloysia is distributed across temperate, subtropical, and desert climates in the Americas.",
